\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Three distinct scalar conditions}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{The invariant weighted value of \ref{fdip-00WM} is defined
by finite addition. The
[normalized coupled coefficient](fdip-00TU) instead
requires its partition coefficient #{Z} to be a unit.
The group projection of \ref{fdip-00WP} requires the
order of its acting group to be a unit. For vertex
gauges that order is #{|G^X|=|G|^{|X|}}.
The positivity conditions for a real probability law
are the separate ones in \ref{fdip-00TX}.}

\p{At characteristic three, the actual
internal column decomposition of \ref{fdip-00VW} for
#{2T} exists although #{24=0} in the coefficient
field. That explicit decomposition does not supply
a group average or an invariant complement in every
module, as the nonsimple example \ref{fdip-00WQ}
illustrates.}
